    <section class="empire-glance" id="at-a-glance" aria-labelledby="glance-title">
      <div class="empire-glance-main"><h2 class="empire-glance-title" id="glance-title">At a glance</h2><ul><li>The Nasrid sultans built the Alhambra as a self-contained royal city, with its greatest palaces raised in the 14th century under Yusuf I and Muhammad V.</li><li>After the surrender of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/granada">Granada</a> in 1492 it became a royal palace of the Spanish Crown, altered and added to by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/charles-v-holy-roman-emperor">Charles V</a>.</li><li>Neglected and damaged in the 18th and 19th centuries, it drew Romantic travellers and has been restored and studied since the 19th century.</li></ul></div>
      <aside class="empire-dyk"><p class="empire-dyk-title">Did you know?</p><p>The tiles of the Alhambra contain nearly all, if not all, of the seventeen mathematically possible wallpaper groups. M. C. Escher's study of them after his visit in 1922 inspired his later work on tessellation.</p></aside>
    </section>

